|name3 = Awakened Urs
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Urs & Minka''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Awakened Urs''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP after completing [[Atonement for Sin]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Urs & Fenrir are very similar to [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]], but have stats between Ururun's Evolved and [[True Form]]s. Overall, Urs is recommended as support for Ururun in stages where the two of them work better than one or as a replacement in stages where Ururun's knockback ability does more harm than good.

==='''True Form'''===
Awakened Urs's stat buffs and range increase are significant improvements to their overall performance. Awakened Urs's stats are now identical to Ururun's True Form, but are generally the superior choice due to the range bonus.

The addition of [[Behemoth Slayer]] and [[Colossus Slayer]] make them a great addition to a lineup whenever these abilities can come into play, increasing their stats by a wide margin and allowing them to rival specialists when against these targets. Additionally, their Behemoth Slayer ability has a '''30%''' dodge chance instead of the usual 5%, giving them an extra layer of defense against [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]] in the event that they reach Urs. Overall, this is a True Form that you will not regret unlocking, but may not have priority over more important True Forms, such as [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Elder Beast Naala]]'s.

